  "valid_2_0": {
    "note": "A complete 2.0 manifest. canonical_json is the exact byte string the COURSE key signed; note the absence of both sig and course_cert. Every key is a fixed ASCII identifier — never a course id, path, or other user-derived string promoted to a key — because a bytewise-sorting Lua JCS and a UTF-16-sorting JS/Kotlin JCS agree only for ASCII. The signed payload carries THREE arrays — files_under_review, ignore and attachments — and JCS leaves array element order alone, so a port that helpfully sorts any of them produces different bytes and a dead signature.",
